Proxmox authentication cache boundaries
=======================================

Shared ticket and live-client cache entries use a process-local keyed digest
of credentials, endpoint, TLS settings and direct/overlay proxy configuration.
The digest does not put plaintext passwords or token secrets into cache keys.
Explicit custom/agent transports bypass shared caches so a ticket cannot move
between sites that happen to use the same appliance address and username.
Repeated requests through an already-open client still reuse its connection.

Closing an older client does not remove a newer cached client. Ticket entries
are pruned after expiry and capped at256 identities. A stale401 invalidates
only its matching cached ticket. Selected API-token authentication never
switches to password login after401; incomplete token configuration fails
closed. Password-mode401 retries retain their existing single re-login rule.

The safe tradeoff is more password-login calls across separate agent-backed
client instances. This is not proof of live appliance compatibility, external
agent delivery, revocation immediacy or concurrent client ownership. Shared
host reachability cooldown and provider discovery error propagation remain
separate reviews. Deploy every serving API/worker process together; old
processes still retain the old unsafe cache behavior.
